# ECommerce Cores Cursor Rule

- Treat SQLite as the source of truth for runtime commerce data.
- Use Entity Framework Core by default.
- Access data through StoreContext and application services.
- Never invent database results.
- Never set databaseChecked=true unless code actually queried the database.
- Do not execute arbitrary user-provided SQL.
- Use async EF Core methods and SaveChangesAsync for mutations.
- Use transactions when one business operation modifies multiple tables.
- Do not place real customer, order, payment, or production database data in Git.
- Keep Product, Stock, Price, Rules, Order, and Payment responsibilities separated.
- Before coding, identify the task ID and relevant core ID.
- After coding, summarize changed files, tests run, and remaining risks.
